\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Temperature does the work; allocation adds full-frame MUSIQ.} (a)\nobreakspace  {}On 187 held-out prompts (seed 0), bars split the gain of SEGA (released){} over NTK{} (dashed: zero; solid: the total, which the bars sum to) into the temperature and base main effects of the 2$\times $2 factorial and the allocation (SEGA (released){} minus SEGA base\,+\,temp.\spacefactor \@m {}); the interaction survives Holm on no metric and is not drawn. Bars are paired mean differences with nominal 95\% prompt-bootstrap intervals; $\star $ marks a Holm-adjusted $p\le 0.05$ over the 80 registered tests. (b)\nobreakspace  {}Illustrative held-out row 32 was chosen by its cabin caption before viewing; native $384^2$ crops (cabin red, mountain cyan) at $(2048,3200)$ and $(2048,1536)$ were fixed after viewing and shared by all arms.\relax }}{1}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:hero}{{1}{1}{\textbf {Temperature does the work; allocation adds full-frame MUSIQ.} (a)~On \N {st@f@n} held-out prompts (seed 0), bars split the gain of \segaofficial {} over \ntk {} (dashed: zero; solid: the total, which the bars sum to) into the temperature and base main effects of the 2$\times $2 factorial and the allocation (\segaofficial {} minus \tempsb ); the interaction survives Holm on no metric and is not drawn. Bars are paired mean differences with nominal 95\% prompt-bootstrap intervals; $\star $ marks a Holm-adjusted $p\le 0.05$ over the 80 registered tests. (b)~Illustrative held-out row 32 was chosen by its cabin caption before viewing; native $384^2$ crops (cabin red, mountain cyan) at $(2048,3200)$ and $(2048,1536)$ were fixed after viewing and shared by all arms.\relax }{figure.1}{}}
